WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.742
Some dreams are pictures. Some are places. And some… are songs.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.306
Mira's mother worked nights. She always came home with a song.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.026
Mom used to hum that song. I haven't heard it in years.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.029
Tonight I will show you a room I have not opened in many years.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.869
Somewhere, a music box was playing.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.057
Whoa. Every jar is singing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:03.231
These are lost lullabies. Songs parents sang, that children forgot they ever heard.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:40.029
It found something. That music box… it's playing our song.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.809
Some songs stay with you, even when you forget the words.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:07.642
Mom was singing. And Dad was pointing at the star. I remember now. I remember his voice.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:13.041
Your dad? Mira… you never talk about him.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:19.264
He went away when I was seven. I think I put the whole dream in a jar so it wouldn't hurt.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:27.023
That is why it ran away. A dream wants to be remembered, even when it is sad.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:53.507
Sad dreams are better forgotten. Give it to me, and the hurt goes away.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.046
No. I want to remember. Even the sad parts.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:37.038
Okay, new rule. When in doubt, sing at him.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.529
That night, the lullaby came home.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:53.978
Two nights left. Mira had found the song. Now she needed the rest of the dream.

